  "body": "## Cause\n\nThe post-merge gate of `3bb6647f6` failed in `mcp_live`, test `ui_link_owner::a_false_server_that_proves_the_token_gets_no_tool_call_when_the_window_has_ended`. The cause is a race between a lock release by a close and a concurrent child process start. Part of it is in the product code of #3995 (PR #4020), and not only in the test.\n\n- On Unix, a `flock` belongs to the open file, not to the descriptor.\n- When a thread starts a child process (`Command::spawn`), the child holds a copy of each descriptor until its `exec` closes it.\n- A close of the lock file during that time does not release the lock.\n- `mcp_live` runs many tests in parallel, and some of them start `camcraft-cli` children. Thus the race occurs often in that binary.\n\nThe two places:\n\n1. **Product code**: `link_owner::owner`. To prove that a window has ended, it takes the free lock and released it only by the close of the file. When a fork occurred at that moment, the lock stayed held. The next lock test then read the ended window as alive, and the CLI dialed its address. This is the defect class that #3995 closes. In a looped run, the CLI dialed the false server of the crashed-window test (`Busy` after the hello timeout).\n2. **Test code**: the tests ended a stand-in window with `drop(lock)`. The CLI's lock test after the hello then saw the lock still held, opened a session and sent the tool call to the false server. The failure text was `Failed(\"... closed the link before it answered\")` at `ui_link_owner.rs:111`.\n\n## What changed\n\n- `link_owner::owner`: after it takes a free lock, it calls `File::unlock` before the close. If the unlock fails, the entry is unproved and is not dialed.\n- `Registration::drop` (a window closes): unlocks after it removed its files.\n- `link::open`: unlocks on the bind-error path.\n- Tests: the new helper `release_lock` ends a stand-in window with an unlock, as the OS does at a process end. Both `ui_link_owner` tests that end a window use it.\n\nNo retry, no sleep and no `#[ignore]`. Decision record: `docs/decisions/4041-ui-link-lock-release.md`.\n\nResidual (in the decision record): when a window process crashes while one of its own threads starts a child, the lock stays held until that child runs `exec`. This is a short time, and the OS ends it.\n\n## Readings\n\nLoop: the whole `mcp_live` binary (25 tests), `--test-threads=24` as on the runner, four loops at the same time for load, from `crates/app`:\n\n- Unchanged binary (`origin/main` `3bb6647f6` tree): 150 runs. `a_false_server_that_proves_the_token_gets_no_tool_call_when_the_window_has_ended` failed in 42 runs. `a_crashed_windows_file_is_removed_and_its_port_is_never_dialed` failed in 2 runs. (These runs used a copy of the binary with no `assets/` beside it, so `live_gate_allows_explicitly_approved_calls_and_never_auto_approves_post_or_machine_edits` also failed in all 150. That is an artifact of the copy, not a result.)\n- Test fix only (the product code unchanged): 200 runs, 1 failure. `a_crashed_windows_file_is_removed_and_its_port_is_never_dialed` returned `Busy`: the CLI dialed the false server. This showed the product defect in `owner`.\n- Final head (the test fix and the product fix): **200 of 200 runs passed**, in place, with no failure in any test.\n\nGate on the final head:\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` (`CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=6`): 3 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled (app build, app lib, `mcp_live`).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Pinning tests: `ui_link_owner::a_false_server_that_proves_the_token_gets_no_tool_call_when_the_window_has_ended` and `ui_link_owner::a_crashed_windows_file_is_removed_and_its_port_is_never_dialed`, pinned by the 200-run loop.\n- Light lane: not run. The diff does not reach the light twins (motion adaptive twins and `pocket_pass_start`), and it changes no post and no toolpath. No heavy step: this is a P2 PR.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Windows and macOS were not run. On Windows, `LockFileEx` belongs to the handle, and std makes handles non-inheritable. The explicit unlock is correct there too.\n- A crash of a real window process during a child start was not emulated (see the residual).\n\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #4041\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
